course: dictionary
lesson: 5702
title: One word, three meanings: lollipop
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A word can have more than one meaning, and the sentence tells you which one is meant. Lollipop usually means a hard sweet on a stick that you lick or suck. «A lollipop or boiled sweet is sugar syrup boiled until almost all the water is gone.»
explain: In the UK and Australia, a lollipop can also be an ice lolly, which is frozen juice on a stick. In the UK, Australia and New Zealand, a lollipop lady or lollipop man is a person who helps children cross the road near school. Look at the other words in the sentence to see which meaning fits.
explain: «Pat the lollipop lady says, Lovely weather for ducks, chuck!» Here lollipop lady is a person, not a sweet, because she says something and helps children cross. The clue is the word lady. Always check: does this meaning make sense in the sentence?
fact: A lollipop is a hard sweet on a stick that you lick or suck.
fact: In the UK and Australia, a lolly can mean an ice lolly: frozen juice on a stick.
fact: A lollipop lady or man helps children cross the road, holding a round STOP sign on a pole.
fact: «Chuck» is a Northern word for «dear», so Pat is being friendly.
fact: «Never run with a lollipop or anything in your mouth, or with sharp things in your hand.» This is a safety rule to stop accidents.
exercise: «Never run with a lollipop or anything in your mouth.» Why is this rule important? | So the lollipop melts faster | Because running is not allowed at all | So you can run faster | *So you do not fall and hurt your mouth or throat
exercise: What is a lollipop lady? | *A person who helps children cross the road near a school | A teacher who gives out sweets | A shop worker who sells ice lollies | A bus driver
exercise: Find and copy the word in «Lovely weather for ducks, chuck!» that is a Northern word for dear. | weather | ducks | *chuck | lovely
test: In the US, a lollipop is often called a... | *sucker | stick | pop | lolly
test: «A lollipop or boiled sweet is sugar syrup boiled until almost all the water is gone, so it sets hard and glassy.» A lollipop is really a kind of... | *sugar glass | sponge cake | water | ice
exam: Why should you brush your teeth after eating a lollipop? | Lollipops make teeth grow | *Sugar can cause tooth decay | Because lollipops are sharp | To make the stick clean
